'' WHICH ROOT OWNS MAIN IS IN THE KEY (PLAN B3): the same two sources in the other order make b
'' main and a a module constructor, so both miss on the 'main' line -- a hit would link two
'' mains, or none -- and the program now runs a's code first.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.ucr/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.ucr
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/unitcache => build/.ucr/src
'' STEP: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.ucr/src/a.tiko build/.ucr/src/b.tiko -o build/.ucr/app.exe
'' ARGS: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.ucr/src/b.tiko build/.ucr/src/a.tiko -o build/.ucr/app.exe -v
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: unit build/.ucr/src/b.tiko: miss (main 1 first 1)
'' EXPECT-OUT: unit build/.ucr/src/a.tiko: miss (main 0 first 0)
'' RUN: build/.ucr/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a top
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b says 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b top
